{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":138194,"duration_api_ms":205609,"num_turns":4,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f08dbbdf-742c-48da-9d10-18650f023d26","total_cost_usd":0.5446024,"usage":{"input_tokens":3036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29208,"cache_read_input_tokens":79946,"output_tokens":2875,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29208,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":179,"outputTokens":10558,"cacheReadInputTokens":1015204,"cacheCreationInputTokens":64428,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23502439999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3036,"outputTokens":2875,"cacheReadInputTokens":79946,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29208,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.309578,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Agreed with planner on all six amendments after independent code verification. The four rejected amendments are either stale (tests already pass with existing gas exchange controls), speculative (tolerance concern not borne out), or design decisions that shouldn't be bundled. The two accepted amendments identify genuine defects: assert_o2_balanced has a real verification gap where incorrect gross splits can pass undetected, and the TANK_BUDGET_DEBUG env var guard has a real isolation defect under Rust's default parallel test harness.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-6-6d614fa3","decision":"reject","rationale":"All four cited tests currently pass. feeding_test_state() already sets reaeration_kla_base=0.0 and aeration.enabled=false. The high-mortality test zeroes KLA terms directly. The reproduction test intentionally keeps reaeration on and accounts for chemistry CO2 flux by subtracting it from the conservation assertion. The failures described in the amendment do not exist in the current codebase."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-d08dd36c","decision":"reject","rationale":"No demonstrated need. Existing tests either close gas exchange entirely via KLA controls (feeding, high-mortality) or explicitly account for CO2 flux in assertions (reproduction). An independent CO2-only toggle creates an unphysical simulation state (O2 exchanges but CO2 does not) and adds ProcessParams surface area without a concrete correctness benefit."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-95b16edc","decision":"reject","rationale":"The reproduction test currently passes at 1e-6 tolerance over 60 days with full subsystem activity, after adjusting for tracked chemistry CO2 flux. The claim that floating-point drift will exceed 1e-6 is speculative and contradicted by the test actually passing. Widening tolerance to 0.1-1.0 mg would mask real conservation leaks. This amendment weakens a valuable regression guard based on a hypothetical."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-c89182dd","decision":"reject","rationale":"There is already an explicit comment at shrimp.rs:263-265 documenting that maintenance respiration is planned for later phases. Reserve is not a pure accumulator—it is drained by mortality (proportional transfer to detritus) and by reproduction (funding new shrimp biomass). Adding a maintenance drain is a substantive biology/calibration change that requires proper design and validation, not a bundled comment-level follow-up."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-ea14338c","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed by code inspection. assert_o2_balanced only validates that inventory_delta equals the sum of recorded net O2 deltas. Oxygen snapshot accounting uses ElementBudget::from_delta() which collapses to a single direction (all in_mg or all out_mg), unlike N/C which track component-level gross flows. The regression test at budget_helpers.rs:348-365 can pass even if a stage's gross in_mg/out_mg split is completely wrong, as long as the net across all stages matches the inventory. This is exactly the class of bug the helper is supposed to catch."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-4c95fd77","decision":"accept","rationale":"Real isolation defect. Rust's default test harness runs tests in parallel (not sequentially as one might assume). The BudgetDebugEnvGuard mutex only serializes callers that explicitly acquire the same lock, but std::env::set_var(\"TANK_BUDGET_DEBUG\", \"1\") modifies the process-global environment. Any concurrently running test that calls step_and_inspect() or checks debug_enabled() will observe the env var without holding the lock. The reported stray debug output under --nocapture confirms order-dependent behavior."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0ded1ccf-1fba-4212-a9d8-7d1aa10e54dd"}
